    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense. With a score of 83.29, **Gunnar Henderson** is our primary engine; his projection is bolstered significantly by a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage against Buehler. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.38) and **Jackson Merrill** (68.43) provide excellent value from the top of the order. **Jackson Merrill** specifically benefits from an elite opportunity to swipe a base against a slow-delivering pitcher, which is a critical consideration given our current scarcity strategy for stolen bases. Both **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** are high-confidence starts as well, with **Andy Pages** sharing the same stolen base upside as **Jackson Merrill** in his matchup against Hudson.\n\nWhile our core is locked in, the most difficult decision involved the final utility spot and the bench. **Miguel Vargas** (43.26) was the odd man out, ultimately falling behind **Josh Jung** (50.08) and **Dominic Smith** (47.21). Although **Miguel Vargas** offers solid secondary upside, his efficiency was suppressed by a poor matchup against Sheehan, leading us to favor the slightly higher-floor production of **Josh Jung** and **Dominic Smith**. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, as their absence remains a significant drag on our potential output.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in our lower-end starts. **Liam Hicks** (42.69) faces the toughest test of the day against Skenes, whose 2.99 xERA makes him an elite arm; while **Liam Hicks** gains a modest boost from his leadoff spot, we must keep a close eye on his actual performance to ensure we aren't wasting game caps on a high-strikeout outcome. Furthermore, **Sam Antonacci** (46.11) is a marginal play against Sheehan; while he carries a respectable xwOBA, his score is severely hampered by a -15% adjustment for the opposing starter's skill. We are banking on the elite production of **Gunnar Henderson** and our high-speed outfielders to carry the weight while we navigate these tougher pitching matchups.",
